WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.224
Teach customer, offer, and delivery out loud once.

00:00:03.224 --> 00:00:04.432
Teaching proves ownership.

00:00:04.432 --> 00:00:08.059
This lesson is about final oral: teach the framework.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:08.865
Explain customer/offer/delivery.

00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:11.685
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.685 --> 00:00:15.715
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:21.759
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:26.192
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:30.624
Stay practical: teach aloud once before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:36.250
Explain the framework to a peer, camera, or friend without notes if you can.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.524
Remember the objective: teach aloud once.

00:00:38.524 --> 00:00:42.693
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:42.693 --> 00:00:47.242
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:47.242 --> 00:00:51.411
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:55.959
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:58.612
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:58.612 --> 00:01:00.128
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:00.448 --> 00:01:03.874
